  "id": "Compound::DB00306 - Gene::2555",
  "verbalization": "Talbutal is likely to interact with Gabra2 through a shared mechanism involving Gaba receptor activity. The evidence suggests that Talbutal binds to Gabra6, Gabrb1, or Gabre, all of which participate in Gaba receptor activity, and Gabra2 is a participant in this activity. This implies that Talbutal may exert its effects through a common pathway involving Gaba receptors, potentially modulating neuronal activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Talbutal in influencing Gaba receptor function, which could contribute to its pharmacological effects. The evidence supports a link between Talbutal and Gabra2 through a mechanism involving Gaba receptor participation, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
